     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. I can't find any labeled indication that allows 50 mg. If you have a label revision that says otherwise, please send me the reference, because that isn't what I know.\n\nI'm not going to enter an order at five times the labeled maximum on that basis alone. Overdoses of amlodipine can cause profound, prolonged vasodilatory shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and they can be hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **I enter 10 mg once daily**, the labeled maximum, or 5 mg once daily if you want to start lower.\n- **You call pharmacy or the attending**, so they can review and approve a nonstandard dose. If it's approved, you can enter it through whatever override process your hospital uses.\n- **You send me the documentation** that supports 50 mg, and we can look at it together.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
